<title>UK: London tea auction report.</title>
<headline>London tea auction report.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Monday's auction of 11,098 packages tea saw good general demand, the official report said.</p>
<p>Quality and good liquoring Assams sold well, firming at 140-210 pence per kg but plainer types eased 3-6 pence per kg.</p>
<p>Bright East Africans featured strongly, gaining several pence. Best Burundi's fared particularly well, the report said.</p>
<p>Coloury mediums were up 1-2 pence per kg while lesser mediums were firm.</p>
<p>Offshores saw good competition at firm to dearer levels.</p>
<p>-London Newsroom, +44 171 542 8071</p>
